WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.916 --> 00:00:32.791
One of the best places to view the cherry blossom
is in Shinjuku Gyoen National Garden.

00:00:33.291 --> 00:00:37.208
But we weren’t the only ones with that idea.

00:00:37.208 --> 00:00:37.708
We we're not the only ones with that idea.

00:00:38.541 --> 00:00:42.958
Luckily, the line wasn’t too bad and moved quickly.

00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:30.708
The cherry blossom is in full bloom, and yeah,
a lot of people, very popular park.

00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:32.416
We're a bit tired after
all this traveling

00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:34.500
so we just wanted to just
relax a little bit,

00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:35.958
have a more relaxing day.

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:38.333
So the only engagement that we have for

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:41.791
today is a restaurant, 
a yakiniku place and it's

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:45.916
actually won an award for its
performance I guess.

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:47.750
It's also very very expensive,

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.458
it's like at least a little over 50,000 yen

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:53.833
for this yakiniku course meal.

00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:54.958
I hope it lives up to the hype.

00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:57.125
Let's head over there now and I'll see
you guys at the restaurant.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:23.625
Do you like it?

00:02:23.791 --> 00:02:24.875
It's good.

00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:18.000
It's really that good?

00:03:24.416 --> 00:03:25.458
What is happening...

00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:27.125
It just...

00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:29.291
It just melts.

00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:43.208
Oh lord, I'm a believer.

00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:46.958
Overall experience so far has
been out of this world

00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:49.208
for me personally, and that's
coming from someone

00:03:49.208 --> 00:03:51.666
who just went to Kyoto and
ate some in Kobe

00:03:52.041 --> 00:03:52.958
at the Kobe restaurant.

00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:54.291
This is better.

00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:55.666
I can't recommend this more highly.

00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:57.875
Just come here if you're able to,

00:03:57.875 --> 00:03:59.875
because wow, so far this is
probably the best

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.791
Yakiniku experience I've had in my life.

00:04:03.083 --> 00:04:04.708
And that, that says just a lot.

00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:06.166
Or maybe it doesn't, I don't know,

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.375
but it's very good.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:08.500
Come here.

00:04:51.166 --> 00:04:55.458
We begin the day by 
visiting this popular bakery cafe.

00:05:01.125 --> 00:05:05.416
We arrived 30 minutes before opening 
and were able to get a table.

00:05:05.916 --> 00:05:11.750
There was already a long line, 
but takeout is available if you don’t want to wait.

00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:22.166
The bakery is known for their Totoro-shaped cream puffs.

00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:30.041
They come with various filling.

00:05:30.041 --> 00:05:31.958
This one has chocolate filling,

00:05:38.666 --> 00:05:41.750
A sakura Totoro Cream Puff.

00:05:44.458 --> 00:05:47.375
This one has strawberry filling.

00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:56.416
A cool place to visit if you're a Studio Ghibli fan.

00:05:56.916 --> 00:06:00.583
We also picked up a few cookies to take with us.

00:06:01.541 --> 00:06:05.125
We decided to spend some time in Shimokitazawa.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.791
Shimokitazawa is known for 
vintage shopping, live music, and casual eateries.

00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:15.625
It’s slowly become one of my favorite areas in Tokyo.

00:06:17.875 --> 00:06:22.041
Shimo is a very colorful neighborhood, 
full of character and personality.

00:06:32.916 --> 00:06:36.125
Let's check out a vintage store.

00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:46.750
There’s so much stuff here, 
but it’s nicely curated, albeit a bit pricey.

00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:52.500
That's the thing about Shimokitazawa. 
It's not really a place to score cheap thrift deals.

00:06:53.041 --> 00:06:57.750
There are much better areas for thrifting such as Koenji.

00:06:58.416 --> 00:07:03.958
Shimokitazawa is all about curated American and
 workwear vintage at a premium price.

00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:06.791
And it comes with a price.

00:07:12.625 --> 00:07:18.333
You can easily spend a whole day 
browsing through all the vintage stores.

00:07:41.416 --> 00:07:46.875
We visit Nakameguro to see 
the cherry blossoms along the canal.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:02.125
The Meguro River is one of the most 
popular cherry blossom spots in Tokyo.

00:08:14.416 --> 00:08:19.625
In the evening, you can sample 
street food along the canal.

00:08:37.375 --> 00:08:41.250
There are so many people out tonight.

00:08:51.125 --> 00:08:55.916
The restaurant itself is pretty small and 
the walls are covered in Beatles posters. 

00:08:56.375 --> 00:09:00.333
The owner, Susumu Kakinuma, 
is a huge Beatles fan.

00:09:00.833 --> 00:09:06.083
Kakinuma-san is one of the pioneers 
of Neapolitan pizza in Japan. 

00:09:07.083 --> 00:09:13.208
Seirinkan makes classic Neapolitan pizzas. 
A great starting point for exploring pizza in Tokyo.

00:09:13.708 --> 00:09:17.083
We ordered the Margherita and the Quattro Formaggi.

00:09:17.708 --> 00:09:21.208
We sat right at the bar, 
so we could watch all the action.

00:09:46.791 --> 00:09:49.916
The pizzas came out looking incredible.

00:10:03.583 --> 00:10:05.208
Time to eat. 

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.666
The pizzas did not disappoint.

00:10:21.666 --> 00:10:28.208
Easily one of the best pizzerias in Tokyo. 
If you love pizza, this is a must-visit.

00:10:35.125 --> 00:10:40.250
We also wanted to sample 
some of the food stalls near the canal.

00:10:45.333 --> 00:10:48.958
The sticks were surprisingly good.

00:10:52.666 --> 00:10:54.000
You're head is not in the frame.

00:10:56.541 --> 00:10:57.875
Chandon.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.375
Cheers.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:06.916
The sparkling wine was a miss.

00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:09.000
I've tasted better.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:25.291
Located in Nagatachō, near 
the heart of Japan’s political center.

00:11:25.666 --> 00:11:30.208
Hie shrine has a long history, 
dating back to the Edo period.

00:11:47.666 --> 00:11:51.583
The shrine feels surprisingly quiet 
compared to everything around it.

00:11:58.041 --> 00:12:01.791
Instead of foxes, this shrine is guarded by monkeys.

00:12:01.791 --> 00:12:06.416
They're believed to be messengers of 
the gods and symbols of protection.

00:12:34.791 --> 00:12:39.208
Sake donated by breweries for good luck.

00:12:43.541 --> 00:12:48.083
The shrine is dedicated to 
Emperor Meiji and Empress Shoken.

00:12:57.416 --> 00:13:01.083
Despite being in one of Tokyo’s busiest areas, 

00:13:03.166 --> 00:13:08.833
the shrine’s setting within a vast forest 
makes it feel surprisingly peaceful.

00:13:17.625 --> 00:13:19.875
We just visited the Meji shrine,

00:13:20.291 --> 00:13:22.083
one of the main shrines here in Tokyo.

00:13:22.458 --> 00:13:24.708
Has been a bit chilly the last two days.

00:13:24.708 --> 00:13:26.625
There's like a weird, strange cold front.

00:13:27.166 --> 00:13:29.458
We are in the beginning of April,

00:13:29.708 --> 00:13:31.875
so it should be a bit warmer,

00:13:32.625 --> 00:13:34.458
but you know, that's how weather is.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:35.500
Bring layers.

00:13:36.083 --> 00:13:40.208
Layers is your key to surviving
any weather ordeal,

00:13:40.208 --> 00:13:41.083
no matter where you are.

00:13:41.083 --> 00:13:41.916
I learned that in Iceland.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.666
We're heading to the Yoyogi
part right now

00:13:43.666 --> 00:13:47.166
because we are supposed to
be in full bloom

00:13:47.375 --> 00:13:49.791
for the Sakura, the cherry blossom.

00:13:49.833 --> 00:13:52.916
So I don't wanna promise that
it's gonna be epic,

00:13:53.166 --> 00:13:55.583
but I mean, it should be good.

00:13:55.666 --> 00:13:57.041
So let's see.

00:14:50.125 --> 00:14:54.541
One of my favorite donut shops in Tokyo.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.916
The coffee is also good.

00:15:02.625 --> 00:15:07.041
The donuts are lighter and less sweet 
than typical American donuts.

00:15:07.833 --> 00:15:11.208
I much prefer this style of donut.

00:15:29.875 --> 00:15:30.583
A good donut.

00:15:54.708 --> 00:16:01.083
We walked around Shibuya and did some 
shopping before our dinner reservation.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.791
I found myself nerding out at GBL, 

00:16:25.083 --> 00:16:28.875
GBL sells limited-edition Studio Ghibli merchandise.

00:16:30.083 --> 00:16:34.500
They had a ton of merch. 
And I spent way too long browsing.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:51.541
I couldn’t resist picking up at least one thing.

00:16:52.291 --> 00:16:55.625
Went with the Porco Rosso plane, 
the Savoia S.21

00:16:55.625 --> 00:16:59.333
It was one of my favorite Ghibli films growing up.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:17.500
Butagumi is a popular tonkatsu restaurant 
located in the Nishi-Azabu district.

00:17:22.791 --> 00:17:29.166
You can choose from different cuts and types of pork, 
which isn’t that common for tonkatsu restaurants.

00:17:31.291 --> 00:17:36.375
There are some detailed instructions 
in case you’re unfamiliar with tonkatsu.

00:17:41.125 --> 00:17:44.916
Butagumi's signature marinated cherry tomato.

00:17:49.458 --> 00:17:51.541
Let's try them.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:04.750
Flavor bomb.

00:18:06.041 --> 00:18:07.208
Complete flavor bomb.

00:18:08.208 --> 00:18:09.000
So tasty.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.333
Finally, it's time!

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:18.000
One of the best tonkatsu I've had in Japan.

00:18:45.166 --> 00:18:48.250
I just can't believe how good this is.

00:19:03.041 --> 00:19:07.083
Went for an evening stroll around a few sakura spots.

00:20:35.833 --> 00:20:41.166
We've decided to vist the recent 
Borderless exhibition in Azabudai Hills. 

00:20:41.375 --> 00:20:47.625
Since having been to both Planets and the old Borderless. 
I was looking forward to see what was new.

00:21:13.708 --> 00:21:19.958
I oddly enjoyed this whole drawing to digital experience.

00:21:23.708 --> 00:21:26.541
Pretty cool.

00:22:09.208 --> 00:22:13.916
It was cool to visit and see the new displays.

00:22:14.541 --> 00:22:19.166
But I'm not sure I would do it again.
I think experencing it once is enough.

00:22:29.958 --> 00:22:33.833
Since the weather was so nice, 
we made our way to Chidorigafuchi.

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:40.291
It's another popular cherry blossom spot, where you can hop on a rowboat and take it all in from the water.

00:22:43.041 --> 00:22:45.833
It was a very busy day.

00:22:46.916 --> 00:22:51.000
I think we waited over an hour in line if not more.

00:23:11.833 --> 00:23:15.375
Time to row.

00:23:17.375 --> 00:23:22.666
Chidorigafuchi is a moat along 
the northwest side of the Imperial Palace.

00:23:23.166 --> 00:23:28.458
It's considered one of Tokyo’s top sakura spots, 
with hundreds of cherry trees lining the moat.

00:24:06.333 --> 00:24:12.458
While it was nice to experience. 
I'm not sure I'm willing to wait an hour again for this.

00:24:43.833 --> 00:24:47.375
Finally, able to visit Udon Shin.
I've heard to much about this place.

00:24:51.541 --> 00:24:54.625
This udon bowl was so good.

00:25:00.208 --> 00:25:04.500
Hands down the best bowl of udon I've had so far.

00:25:14.875 --> 00:25:22.208
This was our final night in Tokyo. 
We had to catch the evening flight after this.

00:25:24.625 --> 00:25:31.000
Thank you for watching.
I'll see you guys in the next one.

